  "36748": {
    "user_line_comment": "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nSteps the player frog (Sprite 0) 1 pixel to the right across the 9-bit VIC-II\nX coordinate ($D010 bit 0 : $D000), clamped at the right playfield boundary\n($0147 / 327), and decrements the hop pixel counter; on the 16th hop pixel,\ncompletes the rightward hop with the landed right-facing sprite ($61). Also\ncalled with a dummy counter (zpa_45 = $02) to carry the frog on right-moving\nriver lanes.\n\nInputs:  $D000 = Sprite 0 X low byte; $D010 bit 0 = Sprite 0 X MSB;\n         zpa_45 = remaining hop pixel counter ($0F..$00, or $02 on river);\n         zpa_48 = 30-frame prescaler count (sampled via finish_frog_hop)\nOutputs: zpa_2D = updated (clamped) Sprite 0 X low byte;\n         zpa_45 decremented ($0E..$FF, or $01 on river carry);\n         mid-hop/river (zpa_45 >= 0): A = zpa_2D, X and Y preserved;\n         when hop completes (zpa_45 == $FF): X = $61, a_47F8 = $61,\n         zpa_79 = $00, A = zpa_5D = zpa_48, Y preserved\nSide Effects: Updates VIC-II Sprite 0 9-bit X position ($D000 and $D010 bit 0);\n              on the 16th hop step, calls finish_frog_hop (writes Sprite 0\n              pointer $47F8 = $61 and reads $D01F to clear latched collisions)\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="
