    "user_line_comment": "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nUnpacks a descriptor of N 8-byte top-half lane glyphs from (zpa_02) into N\nvertically mirrored 16-byte (8x16 top/bottom) character pairs in the selected\nRAM charset, appends one 16-byte background-filled blank character pair ($00\nroad asphalt or $55 river water), and advances the active charset cursor.\n\nInputs:  zpa_02/zpa_03 = 16-bit ROM source pointer (N * 8 top-half glyph bytes);\n         zpa_0A = total source byte count to unpack (N * 8);\n         zpa_1B = target charset selector ($00 = road $5000, non-zero = river $47C0/$4800);\n         zpa_1C/zpa_1D = 16-bit river/top charset write cursor (when zpa_1B != 0);\n         zpa_1E/zpa_1F = 16-bit road/bottom charset write cursor (when zpa_1B == 0)\nOutputs: zpa_1E/zpa_1F (if zpa_1B == 0) or zpa_1C/zpa_1D (if zpa_1B != 0)\n           advanced by (2 * zpa_0A) + $10 bytes;\n         zpa_08/zpa_09 = updated cursor; zpa_06/zpa_07 = updated cursor - $10;\n         zpa_02/zpa_03 = entry source + zpa_0A - 8; zpa_2C = zpa_0A;\n         zpa_2D = $00 or $55; zpa_20 = $08, zpa_21 = $01, zpa_10 = $01,\n         zpa_11 = $00, zpa_12 = $10, zpa_29 = $00, zpa_2A = $00;\n         A = zpa_09, Y = $10; X preserved (caller descriptor index)\nSide Effects: Writes (2 * zpa_0A) + 16 bytes of mirrored 2-row lane tiles and a\n              trailing blank column into RAM ($47C0/$4800 river or $5000 road charset)\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="
