    "user_line_comment": "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nComputes the per-lane 12-step diving-turtle animation phase, selects the\npre-shifted swimming, half-submerged, or underwater ripple tile strip, erases\nthe vacated trailing column, and draws a group of turtles into Screen RAM.\n\nInputs:  zpa_0F = river lane index (0..4; turtle lanes are 1 and 4)\n         zpa_0C = group config byte (bits 0..6 = base col 1..48, bit 7 = dive)\n         zpa_0E = turtles per group (2 or 3)\n         zpa_78 = lane fine horizontal scroll phase (0..3)\n         zpa_B1 = global 30-frame turtle animation phase (0..11)\n         zpf_9D[0..4] = per-lane phase offset (lane 1 = 8, others = 0)\n         zpf_8B[0..8] = per-lane coarse scroll offset (0..49)\nOutputs: zpf_A2[zpa_0F], zpa_30 = lane dive phase (0..11; phase 9 drowns frog)\n         zpa_27 = selected pre-shifted turtle base tile ID\n         zpa_15/$16, zpa_17/$18 = lane top/bottom Screen RAM row pointers\n         zpa_2D = unwrapped group anchor col; zpa_19 = zpa_27 + 8\n         zpa_0B = $00, zpa_14 = $00, zpa_2B = zpa_0E\n         A = zpa_0E, X = zpa_0F, Y = column one step left of drawn group\nSide Effects: Erases trailing water column ($07) and writes zpa_0E * 4 visible\n              2-row turtle columns (0..39) into VIC Bank 1 Screen RAM ($4400)\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="
