    "user_line_comment": "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nGenerates a pre-shifted horizontal scroll copy of a 2-row (16-scanline)\nmulticolor tile strip from (zpa_04) into RAM charset cursor (zpa_08) by\ncircularly rotating all zpa_0A 16-byte column-pairs left or right by A bits,\nthen advances zpa_08/zpa_09 past the generated strip.\n\nInputs:  A = bit-rotation count (2, 4, or 6 bits = 1, 2, or 3 multicolor px)\n         zpa_04/zpa_05 = 16-bit unshifted source strip pointer (preserved)\n         zpa_08/zpa_09 = 16-bit RAM charset destination cursor\n         zpa_0A = strip width in 16-byte (2-char) column-pairs (4..14)\n         zpa_0B = shift direction ($00 = left ROL, non-zero = right ROR)\nOutputs: zpa_08/zpa_09 = entry zpa_08/zpa_09 + (zpa_0A * 16)\n         zpa_2D = strip byte size (zpa_0A * 16); zpa_04/zpa_05 preserved\n         zpa_2C = $00, zpa_2B = zpa_0A, zpa_02/$03 & zpa_06/$07 = last col\n         A = updated zpa_09, X = $09, Y = $10\nSide Effects: Writes zpa_0A * 16 pre-shifted glyph bytes to RAM charset at\n              [entry zpa_08/zpa_09 .. + (zpa_0A * 16) - 1]; uses 3 bytes of\n              hardware stack temporarily (2 for zpa_04/$05, 1 for PHP/PLP)\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="
