    "user_line_comment": "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nStarts or preempts playback of a SID sound/music stream (0..8) when no stream\nis active (zpa_6E == 0) or when the requested stream ID has equal or higher\npriority than the active stream (A >= zpa_6F). Parses the 2-byte stream header\n(tempo period, frequency mode, and active voice count) and advances the stream\npointer (zpa_56/zpa_57) to the 3-byte SID voice setup block.\n\nInputs:  A = requested sound stream ID ($00..$08; higher ID = higher priority:\n             0=hop, 1=lady frog, 2=home bay, 3/4=death, 5=low-time alert,\n             6=game over, 7=round clear, 8=theme)\n         zpa_6E = stream active flag ($00 = idle, $01 = playing)\n         zpa_6F = currently active stream ID ($00..$08)\n         sound_stream_ptr_table = 16-bit sound stream pointer table ($9D6B)\nOutputs: zpa_75 = requested stream ID\n         If accepted: zpa_6F = stream ID, zpa_6E = $01, zpa_73 = $01 (voice init\n         pending), zpa_74 = $01 if preempting an active stream, zpa_56/zpa_57 =\n         stream_base + 2, zpa_70 = tempo, zpa_72 = tempo - 1, zpa_76 = freq mode\n         ($80 direct hi-byte / $00 scaled), zpa_71 = voice count (1..3);\n         A = zpa_57, X = stream_id * 2, Y = $01\n         If rejected (A < zpa_6F while active): active state and X/Y preserved,\n         A = zpa_75, C = 0\nSide Effects: None (SID register updates are deferred to per-frame tick s_9BBA)\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="
